==================== the two whole blind batches on Linux ====================
Same virtual machine (8 virtual CPUs). Third blind photo batch: 16,324 photos (8,628 AI, 7,696 real), 19 sets.
Blind video batch: 2,056 clips (1,156 AI, 900 real), 3 sets. `detect --json --device cpu`, at most 1,200 files per process.
The CPU engine here runs one view per thread (the timings further up were taken before that change, when each
matrix product was split across the threads: 17.4 photos/s on this batch, 24.9 now, the same output to the last bit).
Reference: Community Forensics as its authors ship it (PyTorch 2.15.0, timm 1.0.31, torchvision 0.29.2, 8 loader workers, batch 64)
and its network through this engine ("port"). The three were run one after another on each set.

